  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Immortal Crane Sect he sits on a futon in white robes with a black belt while Lord Sky Crane stands beside him. His face looks young, his green brows reach his waist, and he presses Sky Crane over the lost blood skull Gu, the two juniors who suppressed him, and whether the captured youth is truly the twin of the young man in the recording.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "char_lord_sky_crane",
        "gu_demonic_blood_skull_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears a white robe with a black belt and wide sleeves, sitting on a futon. His face looks like a youngster, smooth as jade. His eyebrows are green and long, extending to his waist, and his eerie dark eyes stare from that face.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Shang Qing pavilion, Lei Tan demands why He Feng Yang defends Fang Yuan when Fang Yuan is not a sect disciple. He Feng Yang answers that even three times the nine-sect compensation cannot compare to Hu Immortal blessed land, let alone fixed immortal travel Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        406
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-dispute",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_qing_pavilion",
        "char_lei_tan",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang says he acknowledged Fang Yuan as Immortal Crane Sect’s man so the other nine sects would drop out, then waits for the sixth earthly calamity to open a loophole and plans kinship pressure through Fang Zheng, trade, and persuasion. If capture still fails he names Slavery Gu among ways to deal with a mortal. Supreme Grand Elder puts him in charge and forces him to hand over his one’s own way Gu for Feng Jiu Ge’s demand.",
      "chapters": [
        407
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "capture-plan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "gu_slavery_gu",
        "gu_ones_own_way_immortal_gu",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Other Gu Immortals already know he holds that Gu and note the heavy price of using it during the inheritance contest.",
      "chapters": [
        375
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "capture-plan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He stays behind the scenes during the earthly calamity to protect elite disciples, block other Gu Masters, and help if Fang Yuan cannot hold.",
      "chapters": [
        419
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "calamity-watch",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later reads Fang Yuan’s material lists with growing apprehension.",
      "chapters": [
        421
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He then faces rockmen trade terms that lift sect pressure while he still wants guts Gu so disciples can enter the blessed land and, over time, plant traps inside it.",
      "chapters": [
        423
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rockmen-trade",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_guts_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After he became a Gu Immortal he joined third supreme elder Lord Tiger Demon’s faction. Lord Tiger Demon had earlier saved both him and the nine palace crane when he chose to sacrifice himself for the crane. After the ambush he returns injured to Fu Hu blessed land, bows for failing expectations, and Lord Tiger Demon’s anger will carries the report to the sect wills.",
      "chapters": [
        704
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "faction-and-rescue",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lord_tiger_demon",
        "loc_fu_hu_blessed_land"
      ]
    }
  ],
